COUNT() : SELECT COUNT(*)
FROM students WHERE age>22;
- how many

SUM(): Add VALUE
SELECT SUM(fees)
FROM students

SELECT SUM(fees) AS total_fees
FROM students



AVG():
SELECT AVG(fees) AS avg_fees
FROM students


MIN():
SELECT MIN(fees) AS min_fees
FROM students


MAX()
SELECT MAX(fees) AS max_fees
FROM students



SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS total_students,
    AVG(age) AS average_age,
    MIN(age) AS youngest_age,
    MAX(age) AS oldest_age
FROM students;


SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS total_students
FROM students
WHERE is_active=true




6. GROUP BY
WHERE
↓
filters individual rows

GROUP BY
↓
puts similar rows into groups

COUNT / AVG / SUM / MIN / MAX
↓
calculates something for each group

SELECT course, AVG(age) AS avg_age
FROM students
GROUP BY course;


SELECT course, COUNT(*) AS active_student
FROM students
WHERE is_active=true
GROUP BY course



7. HAVING:
notes:

WHERE -> filters rows

GROUP BY -> creates groups

HAVING -> filters those groups